  <h2 id="scope">The v1 scope</h2>
  <p>The scope comes from the reviews of the journal plan (<a href={`${J}/01-goal.md`}>§J1.1</a>).
  Each line has its page.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Four calls</b>: <code>Write</code>, <code>Read</code>, <code>Truncate</code> and <code>SetLeader(new, old)</code>. A single writer gets exactly-once writes; with no leader the
      journal is multi-writer and at-least-once. <a href={url("journal/calls/")}>The calls</a>.</li>
    <li><b>Segments</b>: a segment is the run of slots of one acceptor grid. Only a reshape opens
      one. The first leader of the new grid seals the old one. <a href={url("journal/segments/")}>Segments</a>.</li>
    <li><b>Segment records in the matchmakers</b>: one record per segment, changed only by a
      compare-and-set at a majority. <a href={url("journal/matchmakers/")}>Matchmakers and the register</a>.</li>
    <li><b>Quorum everywhere</b>: no step waits for every member of a group. The grids are the
      majority and the partitioned grid. <a href={url("journal/quorums-and-failures/")}>Quorums and failures</a>.</li>
    <li><b>A controller that heals</b>: it replaces lost members and scrubs the copies. In every
      other case it holds and alerts. <a href={url("journal/controller/")}>The controller</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><b>Out of v1</b> (<a href={`${J}/01-goal.md`}>§J1.2</a>): the Phase-1 bypass, the offloader,
  segment rolls on size or age, grids other than the two above, rolling upgrades, a dedup table,
  a second leader, and an unsafe recover. Their rules stay in the docs for the day they come back.</p>

  <h2 id="roles">The roles</h2>
  <p>Each role is a pure state machine. The journal composes the roles of <code>paros-consensus</code> and adds no journal concept to it
  (<a href={`${J}/04-roles.md`}>§J4.1, §J4.3</a>).</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Job</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Batcher, unbatcher</td><td>Multi-writer only: put many writes in one slot, then give each write its own positions.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Leader</td><td>Gives each command a slot, holds each answer until its slot applies, seals the old segment.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Proxy leader</td><td>Runs Phase 2 of one slot on one column of the grid.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Acceptor</td><td>The grid of one segment. Default: one column of three, a plain majority.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Replica</td><td>Applies the slots of its segment in order, folds the journal state, serves reads.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Matchmaker</td><td>Keeps the configuration of each ballot. One set of <code>2F + 1</code> per journal.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Matchmaker register</td><td>An optional role beside the matchmaker: the segment records and the controller term.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Controller</td><td>Elected by a term in the register. Asks for a reshape; never decides safety.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>The roles and their driver follow one contract, the flight rule: each write to disk has an
  id, and each message names the write it waits on. So a driver can group writes and keep many in
  flight, and the role still decides every order (<a href={`${J}/04-roles.md`}>§J4.2</a>,
  checked by <a href={`${TLA}/flight-rule`}><code>flight-rule/</code></a>). The <a href={url("consensus/driver/")}>driver loop</a> page shows the contract of <code>paros-consensus</code> today.</p>

  <h2 id="checked">How it is checked</h2>
  <p>No code before its model (<a href={`${J}/07-verification.md`}>§J7</a>). Each rule has a
  TLA+ check that passes with the rule and a control that fails without it. Then one model composes
  them: <a href={`${TLA}/journal-state`}><code>journal-state/</code></a> runs three segments, the
  seal, partial register writes, the fold and the disk of each acceptor, with a crash between two
  writes. Then the code gets the three judges of the consensus core: each walk of the code is
  checked against the model, seeded walks run with faults on, and a coverage gate asks for every
  branch.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Model</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Exactly-once, multi-writer, a resend across a seal</td><td><a href={`${TLA}/multi-writer`}><code>multi-writer/</code></a>, <a href={`${TLA}/journal-state`}><code>journal-state/</code></a></td></tr>
      <tr><td>The seal end, the boundary state, two seals in a row</td><td><a href={`${TLA}/seal-chain`}><code>seal-chain/</code></a>, <a href={`${TLA}/seal-ctrl`}><code>seal-ctrl/</code></a></td></tr>
      <tr><td>A write reaches only its segment's replicas; retire</td><td><a href={`${TLA}/segment-replicas`}><code>segment-replicas/</code></a></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Segment records across a matchmaker handover</td><td><a href={`${TLA}/segment-records`}><code>segment-records/</code></a></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Quorum everywhere</td><td><a href={`${TLA}/quorum-everywhere`}><code>quorum-everywhere/</code></a></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Damage and repair (CTRL)</td><td><a href={`${TLA}/ctrl-grid`}><code>ctrl-grid/</code></a>, <a href={`${TLA}/ctrl-segments`}><code>ctrl-segments/</code></a></td></tr>
      <tr><td>The controller's election and reshape; health</td><td><a href={`${TLA}/grid-controller`}><code>grid-controller/</code></a>, <a href={`${TLA}/health`}><code>health/</code></a></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>§J7.1 maps every rule to its model. The <a href={url("engineering/")}>safety case</a> lists each claim of the journal with its model, its walk and its state: checked on the code, model only, or open. <a href={url("journal/checks/")}>How it is checked</a> explains every technique in one page.</p>

  <h2 id="code">In paros</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={`${REPO}/tree/main/crates/lib/paros-journal`}><code>paros-journal</code></a>: the
      pure journal core. The fold (<code>JournalState</code>), the <code>resolve</code> call, the held
      answers, the segment record (<code>SegmentRecord</code>), the matchmaker register
      (<code>register</code>) and the codec.</li>
    <li><a href={`${REPO}/tree/main/crates/sim/journal-sim`}><code>journal-sim</code></a>: seeded
      walks of the fold over a chain of segments and of the register across handovers, oracles with
      no shared code, and the trace check of each walk against <code>journal-state/FoldTrace.tla</code>
      and <code>segment-records/RegisterTrace.tla</code>.</li>
    <li>Not built yet: the journal roles (#1326), the controller
      (<code>paros-journal-control</code>, #1328), the driver (<code>paros-journal-io</code>, #1329),
      the moonpool adapter (#1330) and the client (#1331). The steps are <a href={`${J}/08-build-steps.md`}>§J8</a>.</li>
  </ul>

